//! Raw Rust bindings for [STP](https://github.com/stp/stp), the Simple Theorem
//! Prover -- an SMT solver for the quantifier-free theories of bit-vectors,
//! arrays and floating point.
//!
//! The bindings are generated by [`bindgen`](https://crates.io/crates/bindgen)
//! from STP's 3.x C API header (`stp/stp.h`) by the build script; nothing in
//! this module is written by hand. The generated items are exposed through
//! [`ffi`].
//!
//! # Building and linking
//!
//! By default the `vendor` feature is enabled. In that configuration the build
//! script downloads (or reuses) STP, builds its 3.x library as a **static**
//! library through the [`cmake`](https://crates.io/crates/cmake) crate, merges
//! the resulting archives plus their dependencies into one `libstp_sys.a`, and
//! links it into the crate. This requires a C++ toolchain, `libclang` (for
//! bindgen) and network access the first time; see `build.rs` for the
//! environment variables that override the source, build and dependency
//! locations.
//!
//! Disabling `vendor` (`default-features = false`) makes the build script link
//! against an STP 3.x installation already present on the system instead,
//! located with `STP_SYS_PREFIX` / `STP_SYS_LIB_DIR` / `STP_SYS_INCLUDE_DIR`.
//!
//! # Ownership model
//!
//! STP's API is split into a term manager (`stp_tm`) and one or more solvers
//! (`stp_solver`). Terms (`stp_term`) and sorts (`stp_sort`) are interned in a
//! manager; a handle returned by a constructor carries one reference owned by
//! the caller. Every fallible function returns a handle (`NULL` on error) or an
//! `stp_status`. The first error is recorded on the manager and can be read
//! with `stp_tm_error`; strings and buffers returned as `char*` are owned by
//! the caller and must be released with `stp_free`.
//!
//! Managers and solvers are not thread-safe: one thread at a time may use a
//! manager and the solvers over it.

pub mod ffi {
	//! The bindgen-generated translation of STP's 3.x C API (`stp/stp.h`).

	#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]
	#![allow(non_snake_case)]
	#![allow(non_upper_case_globals)]
	#![allow(dead_code)]
	#![allow(improper_ctypes)]
	#![allow(clippy::all)]

	include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/bindings.rs"));
}

